// Character voices and reusable field services, authored for the road/fort pass.
const voices=[
 ['TRN-RT-001','I used to watch this bend for sledges, before the road carried soldiers. My sister still brings hot broth from Civeton. I keep the snow clear so someone can always get home. Let me see how you look after your partners.','You kept your head. That matters more than a polished uniform. Follow the beaten snow; the grass hides more than cold roots.','My sister says the town feels emptier every morning. If you find your friends, bring them home together.'],
 ['TRN-RT-002','They issued this coat to someone taller. I have sewn the sleeves twice already. Agnes de Clare says a recruit should learn to listen before learning to shout orders. My partners are helping me practise.','They listened to you even when we pressed hard. I need to earn that sort of trust, instead of expecting it because I have a badge.','Matilda knows this road better than the officers do. Ask her about the carts that went ahead.'],
 ['TRN-RT-003','These boundary stones once marked whose turn it was to repair the road. Now everyone treats them like a wall. My father laid three of them. I still check both sides for travellers who need help.','Father would have offered you water, whichever banner you carried. There is a little shade further on; let your partners rest before the tunnels.','I hear the same worries from both sides of the border. Strange how the banners make them sound different.'],
 ['TRN-RT-004','I have walked this scrub for seventeen summers. The new recruits see an enemy behind every rock. I see tracks, a drying spring and a road that still has to carry bread. Show me you can read a situation.','You knew when to press and when to protect. Keep that judgement when someone with a louder voice gives you an order.','The wind covers footprints overnight. Write down what you actually saw before somebody tells you what it meant.'],
 ['TRN-RT-005','When the armies march overhead, the drains fill with everything they leave behind. My partners and I clear it before the wells turn foul. Nobody sings about that work. We still do it.','Good work. Keep your boots off the broken channels. A clean well is worth more than whatever medals they are handing out upstairs.','If you smell fresh water under all this, follow it to the service keeper. He knows which pipes still feed the town.'],
 ['TRN-RT-006','These keys belonged to my mother. She kept the passage open during the last flood, even when both gates were ordered shut. I am supposed to guard it now. I would rather know who I am letting through.','You care about the partners following you. That is enough for me. Take the passage, and leave the way clear for the next traveller.','Mother used to say a locked gate cannot tell a soldier from a child. The keeper has to make that choice.'],
 ['TRN-RT-007','The ridge wind carries voices further than people think. Yesterday I heard a caravan singing to stop its youngest passengers crying. We escorted them until dawn. My partners have scarcely slept, but they will stand with me.','You have earned the road. There is shelter below the ridge; use it before the wind steals the warmth from your partners.','I keep a ribbon from every caravan that reaches safety. It is a better record than the patrol ledger.'],
 ['TRN-RT-008','I carried spice along this road before I carried a shield. Now the wagons hold bandages, flour and people who have lost their homes. My partners know every wheel rut. Let us see whether you can keep pace.','You would make a fine escort. Stay with the slowest member of your party; a caravan is only safe when its last wagon arrives.','When the road opens again, I will sell spice. I refuse to let this uniform be the last thing my grandchildren remember.'],
 ['TRN-RT-009','I write down the names of everyone who passes. Not for an arrest list. When families come looking, someone ought to be able to tell them which direction their people took. Your partners travel under your care. Show me what that means.','I will record that you passed safely, partners beside you. If someone asks after you, I will have something better to offer than a rumour.','Names, dates, directions. Small things, until they are all a family has left.'],
 ['TRN-RT-010','This satchel has crossed the forest more times than I have counted. The hospice needs its medicine before sunset. My partners clear the path, but they are patients too when the day is done. Keep this challenge careful.','You noticed when your partners needed room to breathe. The wards could use more people who pay attention like that.','The nurses put a little fruit in my bag for the road. I pretend not to notice so they can keep pretending they have enough.'],
 ['TRN-RT-011','I came to volunteer for one afternoon. That was three months ago. There is always another blanket to wash, another frightened partner to settle. Mine stay close when the wards grow loud. Let us work through a challenge together.','There is patience in the way you give orders. Keep it. Fear spreads quickly through a party, but so does calm.','The orchard keepers have started sending fruit again. You should see how a fresh peach changes a whole ward.'],
 ['TRN-RT-012','The seal on this case matters less than the people waiting for it. I have been told to turn back twice today. My partners and I are going through. Prove you can travel beside medicine without putting it at risk.','You understand what we are protecting. If the path floods, keep the medicine high and follow the raised stones.','The nurses never ask which banner a patient carried. I wish more officers would visit the wards.'],
 ['TRN-RT-013','The marks on my staff are flood heights, not victories. That notch is where the old ferry vanished. My partners found three families stranded that night. We still check the shallows when the river looks quiet.','Steady work. Water can rise while you are watching a battle. Keep your return path in sight, and do not mistake a calm surface for safe ground.','I used to teach children to fish here. When the water settles, I intend to start again.'],
 ['TRN-CAVE-1','My brother and I used to haul nets off this coast. He thought the drowned garrison would buy us a new boat. Now I mend ropes for strangers and count every person who comes back up. Earn a descent, and make sure I can count you twice.','The rope is yours. Test each knot before you trust it; I would rather lose my salvage than another person to these stairs.','Freya keeps clean bandages near the gatehouse. Let her look at your partners before you go deeper.'],
 ['TRN-CAVE-2','The pay chest is bronze, but I am looking for the names scratched into it. My grandmother said her father served here. I would like to take home something that proves he was a person, not just a name in a war song.','You can take the next stair. If you find a marked fitting, leave the inscription intact. Someone may still be looking for that name.','Salt eats iron quickly. It takes longer to erase a family story.'],
 ['TRN-CAVE-3','A silver buckle will feed us for a week. That sounds mercenary until you see how little the buyers offer for wet rope and broken tools. My partners haul the heavy pieces. They eat before I do.','First pick downstairs is yours. I will stay with the lighter fittings; my smallest partner has done enough carrying today.','The claws I heard were real. There is a difference between being poor and being foolish; I am not following that noise.'],
 ['TRN-CAVE-4','The reliquary doors were sealed from the inside. I have spent all morning wondering who shut them, and who they left outside. My partners do not like these halls. I trust that feeling more than the salvage map.','Take the last rope. I am keeping my lantern pointed at the stairs; if you turn back, you will have a light to follow.','I will take a rubbing home instead of breaking the seal. Some things deserve to remain where someone left them.'],
 ['TRN-CAVE-5','I promised my daughter a carved shell from the old cistern. Now I would give up the whole haul to be back at her table. My partners are tired. One quick challenge, then we both keep a clear way out.','The path is yours. I am packing the offerings back into their box. My daughter can have a shell from a safer beach.','If something comes up those stairs, I am leaving the pack. My partners are coming with me.'],
 ['TRN-FORT-DORELEM-1','My watch begins where the town ends. Some mornings the people outside ask me for bread; other mornings they throw stones. I still open the little gate for both. The great gate is another matter. Prove your strength here.','I yield the gate. Remember the people beyond these walls when you reach Yusuf; they live with whatever decision is made inside.','My watch continues. A cleared challenge need not become another grudge.'],
 ['TRN-FORT-DORELEM-2','These counterweights are older than our banners. I helped restore them after a flood when True Light masons worked beside ours. Now I am ordered to hold the hall against their children. Show me what yours have learned.','The inner watch yields. The stones will stay where you set them; I have no wish to make you prove the same thing twice.','I still know the masons by name. A uniform has never made that knowledge disappear.'],
 ['TRN-FORT-DORELEM-3','Yusuf put me in charge of these halls because I remember every guard who has stood in them. I intend to remember the ones who leave as well. Prepare your partners. I will not make this easy.','I yield. When you enter the leader’s hall, carry your judgement as carefully as you carried your partners through mine.','The watch is standing down. Let surrender mean something.'],
 ['TRN-FORT-PHILOMERE-1','The garden outside feeds the wards. We train beside it so every recruit remembers what this chapter protects. My partners know the gardeners better than the officers. They will still defend this gate.','The gate is yours. Leave the garden paths clear; the medicine carts use them even when the banners change.','I have seeds drying in my locker. There will be another spring, whoever commands this hall.'],
 ['TRN-FORT-PHILOMERE-2','The relic at my belt is a nurse’s bell. It called this chapter to a plague ward long before it called anyone to battle. I carry it so I remember which duty came first. Face the inner watch.','I yield the passage. Listen for the ward bells when you go on. They are asking for help, not announcing a victory.','My partners can tell a ward bell from an alarm. I wish the council remembered the difference.'],
 ['TRN-FORT-PHILOMERE-3','Aisha remembers which families donated the hospice beds. I remember which guards carried them upstairs. This chapter is full of people who did useful things before they were made enemies. Come prepared; I protect them all.','The captain yields. Your next decision reaches beyond this room, into every bed in the hospice. Give those people a place in it.','We will not challenge you again. The patients still need tomorrow’s medicine.']
];
export const FIELD_VOICES=Object.fromEntries(voices.map(([id,before,after,repeat])=>[id,{before,after,repeat}]));
export function installFieldVoices(expansion,target){Object.assign(target,FIELD_VOICES);for(const t of expansion.trainers)if(FIELD_VOICES[t.id])t.portraitId=t.id;}
export function healFortParty(state){let count=0;for(const u of state.party){if(u.hp<=0||u.dead)continue;u.hp=u.maxHp;u.status=null;u.confusion=0;u.stages={};for(const m of u.moves)m.left=m.pp;count++;}return count;}
export const CACHE_LORE={
 marchMeadow:'The nest keeper has wrapped the bread in clean wool. A note asks travellers to leave the shelter warm for the next hatchlings.',
 burrowHollow:'Survey marks cover the lid. The supplies were set aside for crews who failed to return before dark.',
 glassSluice:'A mineral keeper has sealed the package against the spray. Under the wax is a careful list of the pools still safe to drink from.',
 emberQuarry:'The forge crew left their tools in order, as though they meant to come back after supper. Someone has kept their emergency stores dry.',
 stormBluffs:'A cliff watcher has tied the chest to a stone. The lid bears the names of caravans brought safely down from the ridge.',
 orchardCanopy:'Fruit stains mark the packing cloth. The old orchard stamp has been crossed out and replaced with a handwritten hospice address.',
 reedSanctuary:'The reed wardens left a map of clean springs inside the lid. Several old wells are crossed out in red.',
 coralGrotto:'The tide scholar has weighted this bundle above the high-water line. The knots are the same ones used on the fishing boats outside.',
 moonlitDepths:'Waterproof pages lie under the supplies: sketches of sleeping Abyssals, with a warning to let them wake in their own time.',
 relicCrags:'The shellstone crew has packed each fragment separately. A note asks the next scholar to record where a piece was found before carrying it away.'
};
